    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras head into August 14th with a lineup anchored by **Yordan Alvarez**, who provides our highest ceiling at a 71.66 score. Despite facing a tough arm in George Kirby, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.464 xwOBA that keeps him in must-start territory. **Caleb Durbin** also represents a primary objective today; while his 64.84 score is solid, his presence is prioritized due to the \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor against Bubba Chandler, which provides a key boost to his stolen base potential\u2014a critical strategic pillar for our 5x5 Roto standing. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (59.32) remains a high-leverage start, as his leadoff spot and favorable matchup against Matthew Liberatore outweigh the minor penalty from adverse wind conditions.\n\nPlatoon advantages are driving the bulk of our secondary production. **Dillon Dingler** (56.52) receives a significant +14% boost from a dynamic platoon edge against the lefty Sean Newcomb, making him a much more efficient play than his base projection would imply. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (58.71) is another beneficiary, as the matchup against Steven Matz elevates his floor significantly. Conversely, we are mitigating risk with **Gary Sanchez** and **Kazuma Okamoto**, both of whom are forced to navigate the high-skill barrier of Gerrit Cole and Yoshinobu Yamamoto; while their scores are middling, they remain the optimal pivots given the current roster construction.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Colt Keith** (45.63), who fell just shy of the lineup threshold. While his park factors in a matchup against Sean Newcomb were enticing, the optimizer ultimately penalized him for the L/L platoon disadvantage and the priority we placed on maximizing SB opportunities elsewhere. As a final note, we are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for the entire squad; should any of **Junior Caminero** or **Lars Nootbaar** experience a drop in the batting order, their effective scores will need to be re-evaluated against the bench depth of **Nelson Velazquez** and **Chase Meidroth** to ensure we aren't burning game caps on suboptimal lineup positions.",
